ence/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents SHM is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn the above case:\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "370351b4133d4ba5220f8044d94246ad417420f7548e3be392bed7d50887d919"} {"question" "q-94267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{″}+16{y}^{′}=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+8y=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}-3y=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{4}y=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The function $y(t)$ gives the position of a particle at time $t.$ Which of the following equations represents a situation in which the particle is undergoing simple harmonic motion?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see that the only equation that represents SHM is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2y=0.\n$$\n\nIn the above case:\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=2\\,⟹\\,\\omega =\\sqrt{2}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "370351b4133d4ba5220f8044d94246ad417420f7548e3be392bed7d50887d919"} {"question" "q-94263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{″}+1=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+2y=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+2y=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}-2y=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{″}+2y=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-79485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with simple harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+36y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the oscillation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-79485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=36\\,⟹\\,\\omega =6.\n$$\n\nThe period $T$ is given by:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\omega }\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the period (in seconds) is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{6}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-79485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "370351b4133d4ba5220f8044d94246ad417420f7548e3be392bed7d50887d919"} {"question" "q-79485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-79485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\,\\text{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-79485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-64221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with simple harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the oscillation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-64221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=16\\,⟹\\,\\omega =4.\n$$\n\nThe period $T$ is given by:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\omega }\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the period (in seconds) is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-64221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "370351b4133d4ba5220f8044d94246ad417420f7548e3be392bed7d50887d919"} {"question" "q-64221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-64221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi \\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{s}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\,\\text{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-64221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with simple harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+144y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the oscillation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The simple harmonic motion (SHM) equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=144\\,⟹\\,\\omega =12.\n$$\n\nThe period $T$ is given by:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{\\omega }\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the period (in seconds) is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{12}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/state.json" "file_sha256" "d34deaaaac5100f9d2170d30e24e7b9b26f4fa8a6ba8c769fe9c56391c8c8785"} {"question" "q-94274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14064220/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "370351b4133d4ba5220f8044d94246ad417420f7548e3be392bed7d50887d919"} {"question" "q-94274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mat